\begin{align*}XY^2 &= CY^2 + XZ^2 \\ 12^2 &= h^2 + 6^2 \\ h^2 &= 108 \\ h &= \sqrt{108} = 6\sqrt{3}\end{align*}
Therefore, the area of triangle $XYC$ is $6\sqrt{3} \cdot 6 / 2 = 18\sqrt{3}.$

