\begin{align*}16 \cdot 6\sqrt{3} + 2 \cdot (18\sqrt{3}) & = 96\sqrt{3} + 36\sqrt{3} \\ & = 132\sqrt{3}.\end{align*}
Thus, the surface area of solid $CXYZ$ is $132\sqrt{3}.$ </think> $132\sqrt{3}$

